# Repository-level ignores. The backend and frontend each carry their own generated by Spring
# Initializr and Vite; this file covers what escapes both of them, which is mostly anything created
# at the repository root.

# Secrets. Every credential this project uses comes from an environment variable, but nothing stops
# someone putting one in a file while getting a deployment working and then committing it. .env was
# previously committable, and a leaked database password or JWT signing key is not something that
# can be undone by rotating it quietly.
.env.*
*.env
!.env
!.env.example

# IntelliJ. The backend/.gitignore covers backend/.idea only, which is why the root .idea was tracked:
# it names one developer's JDK build (openjdk-26) and points at a pom.xml that does not exist here.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Other editors and operating systems.
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Build output, in case a build is ever run from the root rather than from backend/ or frontend/.
target/
dist/
node_modules/